# Binary assets that git's content heuristic can still read as text — a PDF
# with no NUL byte in its first 8 KB is the usual offender. Without this, a
# clone with core.autocrlf=true rewrites their line endings, which shifts a
# PDF's xref offsets and silently corrupts the file.
*.pdf   binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.pptx  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.bin   binary
*.yuv   binary
